# Migrations are source, not build output.
#
# A global ignore of `*.sql` kept 120 of these out of the repo, which is
# invisible locally - the files are on disk, every deploy from a laptop works -
# and fatal from CI, whose checkout only has what git tracks. The deploy drops
# the schema and rebuilds it from these files, so a partial set rebuilt a
# partial database: `migrate:fresh` reported "0 applied - no migration files
# found?", and the seed then died on `no such table: csa_plans`.
#
# A negation here rather than `git add -f` each time, because the next
# generated migration would be ignored again and nobody would notice until the
# next deploy from somewhere that is not this machine.
!*.sql
